# Accepted image-scan findings, one identifier per line, each
# preceded by a comment with the reason and a review date (`# review: YYYY-MM-DD`).
# This file is used only for the application image. Database and Dockerfile
# scans intentionally run without these application-specific exceptions.
#
# The pull-request gate (ci.yml `image-scan`) fails on any unlisted CRITICAL or
# HIGH finding that has a fix available. The nightly workflow
# (image-scan-nightly.yml) additionally fails on unfixable ones, so base-image
# exposure with no upstream patch is surfaced daily rather than silently passed.
#

# Every entry below is a Debian 13 package finding with no fix available when
# SEC-004 was written. The runtime is non-root (www-data), read-only,
# `cap_drop: ALL` and `no-new-privileges`, so privileged-mount and setuid
# paths cannot be reached. These reasons rest on those runtime flags (mount
# and su stay setuid in the image), and the file also applies to the db and
# backup scans. Review again before the date shown, or earlier when
# Debian ships a fix, and delete the entry then.

# review: 2026-12-31
# util-linux family (util-linux, mount, login, bsdutils, libmount1, libblkid1,
# libuuid1, libsmartcols1, liblastlog2-2): the four CVEs concern privileged
# mount helpers, nsenter and X-mount options. The container has no
# CAP_SYS_ADMIN, no setuid escalation and never runs mount or nsenter; the
# application neither calls these binaries nor links the libraries for mounts.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# review: 2026-12-31
# libxml2: used by PHP only to read XML the operator provides through console
# commands (workbook migration). No web route parses untrusted XML, request
# bodies are JSON capped at 1 MB, and the process makes no outbound internet request.
CVE-2026-6653
CVE-2026-74860
CVE-2026-86138
CVE-2026-86139
CVE-2026-86140
CVE-2026-86142
CVE-2026-86143
CVE-2026-86144

# review: 2026-12-31
# libcurl4t64: the PHP curl extension is loaded but the application never
# calls it or makes outbound HTTP requests; the curl CLI is purged.
CVE-2026-12064
CVE-2026-8458

# review: 2026-12-31
# libsystemd0 and libudev1: linked by system libraries only; no systemd or
# udev daemon runs in the container and no device access is granted.
CVE-2026-16742

# review: 2026-12-31
# ncurses (libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin): terminal library never used
# by the web process and no interactive terminal is attached in production.
CVE-2025-69720

# review: 2026-12-31
# libacl1: ACL helper used by dpkg and coreutils; the application never sets
# or reads ACLs and the file system is read-only.
CVE-2026-54369

# review: 2026-12-31
# perl-base: required by dpkg and cannot be removed. The affected module
# (Archive::Tar) is never run, and no process in the container invokes perl.
CVE-2026-9538
